          <div class="vertical-card vertical-card--soon">
            <div class="vertical-dot"></div>
            <div class="vertical-name">{v.name}</div>
            <div class="vertical-blurb">{v.blurb}</div>
            <div class="vertical-cta">Coming soon</div>
          </div>
        )
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 05 PRICING -->
  <section class="screen screen--scroll" id="pricing" data-marketing-index="6">
    <div class="eyebrow">PRICING</div>
    <div class="pricing-block">
      <h1 class="hero serif" style="font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,72px);">Build once.<br />Keep it <span class="tint-gold">running well.</span></h1>
      <div class="pricing-tiers">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:14px;">BUILD</div>
          <div class="serif" style="font-size:clamp(28px,3.2vw,44px);">{CURRENCY}{PRICING.buildFirst}</div>
          <p class="sub" style="max-width:340px;">First module. 30-calendar-day working-build commitment from deposit.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:14px;">ADDITIONAL MODULE</div>
          <div class="serif" style="font-size:clamp(28px,3.2vw,44px);">{CURRENCY}{PRICING.buildAdditional}</div>
          <p class="sub" style="max-width:340px;">Each additional module, within the same 30-day window.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:14px;">DEVSHOP CARE + OPTIMISATION</div>
          <div class="serif" style="font-size:clamp(28px,3.2vw,44px);">{CURRENCY}{PRICING.careMin}<span style="font-size:16px; opacity:0.6;">/mo</span></div>
          <p class="sub" style="max-width:340px;">Floor, not the price — depends on what the system actually needs to stay useful.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="module-def">
        <p class="module-def-label">What's a module?</p>
        <p class="module-def-intro">One priced unit of work — a defined function of your business, decomposed to its actual tasks using PTM<sup>&trade;</sup>, our Process / Task / Machine framework, and mapped to a working mechanism. Every module includes:</p>
        <div class="module-def-grid">
          <div class="module-def-item"><span class="module-def-item-title">The team, named</span><span class="module-def-item-body">Role-by-role, hours behind the price — not a black box.</span></div>
          <div class="module-def-item"><span class="module-def-item-title">Human vs. AI, decided per task</span><span class="module-def-item-body">Every task classified Manual, Semi-Automated, Automated, or Fully AI-driven — never automated by default.</span></div>
          <div class="module-def-item"><span class="module-def-item-title">A subject matter expert</span><span class="module-def-item-body">In your industry and this specific business function.</span></div>
          <div class="module-def-item"><span class="module-def-item-title">A functioning app</span><span class="module-def-item-body">Live, connected to your real tools — not a prototype.</span></div>
          <div class="module-def-item"><span class="module-def-item-title">Training &amp; handoff</span><span class="module-def-item-body">We walk your team through it directly at launch.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sub" style="margin-top:28px;">Genuinely complex or custom systems are human-priced after a short scoping call, not forced into the standard tiers.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:40px;"><button class="btn" data-go="intake">Start →</button></div>
